
{"id":"07ed723f-e020-46f4-9a9b-2b5527c3a294","object":"chat.completion","created":1785001503,"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    text = case['text']\\n    passes = case['passes']\\n    max_rounds = case['max_rounds']\\n    current_text = text\\n    applications = []\\n    fixed_point = False\\n    for _ in range(max_rounds):\\n        changed = False\\n        for p in passes:\\n            name = p['name']\\n            old = p['old']\\n            new = p['new']\\n            if old in current_text:\\n                current_text = current_text.replace(old, new)\\n                applications.append(name)\\n                changed = True\\n        if not changed:\\n            fixed_point = True\\n            break\\n    return {'applications': applications, 'fixed_point': fixed_point, 'text': current_text}\"}","reasoning_content":"We need to parse the problem. The task is SE-CR-01. The output must be a JSON object with keys \"applications\" (array of strings), \"fixed_point\" (boolean), \"text\" (string). The solve function takes a case payload. The payload has fields: text, passes, max_rounds, _case_nonce. The passes are a list of objects with name, old, new. Need to simulate repeated application of substitutions until either no more changes or max_rounds reached. The \"applications\" should be the list of names of passes that were applied in order? Or the list of names of passes that actually changed something each round? Need to interpret. The fixture shows three cases with same inputs. The output schema: applications array of strings. Probably the list of pass names that were applied in each round? But there is also fixed_point boolean indicating whether the process reached a fixed point (no further changes) within max_rounds. And text is the final text after applying.\n\nWe need to simulate: start with text. For each round (up to max_rounds), iterate through